{
  "description": "config.v2 §2.15: what the record, a reply, the change event, the error form and a log line carry for a sensitive value, on the test contract `contracts/rfcfg.v1.toml`, whose group sim holds pin, sensitive, beside attempts. Written by an independent reading of the text (Python, standard library), checked, never blessed. A case gives the owner's setup as lifecycle.json writes it, and one call on sim: `fields`, a SetSim or a Control, `hex` its payload, and device_words, what the device says refusing it (or null). expect.sim is sim's part of the Record as the reply, or else the owner's state, carries it: each field of the Record whose name begins `sim__`, by its JSON reading (pin has a source and nothing more: no differs and no value field exist); expect.reply the reply as lifecycle.json writes one; expect.edits the change event's edits, or null when there is no event; expect.log the request as the owner logs it, its JSON reading with each sensitive value written \"<redacted>\". `same_bytes` pairs two setting different PINs, whose records are equal byte for byte: no bit of the record depends on the value.",
